WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.470
A lot goes into rating a film.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:06.470
The Motion Picture Association of America
thoroughly reviews upcoming releases to see

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.280
if they contain content generally deemed inappropriate
for younger audiences.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:15.440
Dirty jokes, mature themes, graphic violence,
and gratuitous nudity can all earn a film

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.260
an R rating, letting parents know they probably
don't want to bring the whole family.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.769
For the most part, this system works well,
but it definitely isn't perfect - as highlighted

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:28.400
by these standout cases of super scary movies
that somehow avoided an R rating.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:30.500
Ouija: Origin of Evil

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.220
From director Mike Flanagan, 2016's Ouija:
Origin of Evil reveals the blood-chilling

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:38.730
events that occurred before the first Ouija
film.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.570
It follows single mom Alice as she runs a
sham psychic business out of her home with

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.530
her daughters Paulina and Doris.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:48.230
When Alice brings a Ouija board into the mix
in an effort to liven up her act with some

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:53.030
supernatural flair, the three women unwittingly
make contact with an evil spirit.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.790
Ouija: Origin of Evil shies away from gore,
but it maintains a constant sense of dread,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.230
delivering violent deaths, a freaky demonic
possession, and enough horrifying images to

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.520
keep you wide awake at night.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.760
Just like we couldn't believe this prequel
was actually a solid film following its vapid

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.820
predecessor, we're also stunned it snuck into
theaters without an R rating.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.440
"And the last thing you feel is cold."

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.280
Mama

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:26.160
2013's Mama stars Jessica Chastain as Annabel
and Nikolaj Coster-Waldau as her boyfriend

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.869
Lucas and follows Lucas' young nieces, Victoria
and Lilly, and the ghostly figure they call

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:32.760
"Mama" that looms over them.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:36.880
When Lucas and Annabel bring Victoria and
Lilly home after they spent five years in

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.649
isolation following their mother and father's
deaths, Mama extends her monstrous maternal

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:45.469
hand beyond the girls' reach to grip the lives
of those around them.

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:50.000
Mama's eerie imagery, tense and terror-filled
story, and haunting ending gives us a case

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.840
of the heebie-jeebies usually reserved for
R-rated fare.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.120
How it skated by on a PG-13 instead, we'll
never fully understand.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:04.400
[spooky monster groaning]

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.540
Insidious

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:11.039
Patrick Wilson and Rose Byrne lead 2010's
Insidious as married couple Josh and Renai

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:14.420
Lambert, who recently moved into a new home
with their three children.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:18.580
What should be a humble abode instead becomes
the center of their nightmares as really bad

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.060
things begin to befall the Lamberts.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.650
It all starts when Josh and Renai's son Dalton
slips into a coma-like state after he sees

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.090
a figure hiding in the attic, and it only
gets worse from there.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.000
After Renai is attacked and a bloody handprint
is left on Dalton's bed, the Lamberts pack

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.200
up and move to a new house - but the spirits
haunting them persist.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.790
A demonic, Darth Maul-looking entity stalks
the family of five, and viewers soon learn

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.890
the real reason for Dalton's unconsciousness
and the startling truth behind Josh's identity.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.519
Insidious is light on blood and guts, but
heavy on creepy imagery, psychological tension,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.720
and unsettling storylines, which is why it's
so surprising that it didn't receive an R

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:54.220
rating.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.480
[Demonic roar]

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.040
"It's here!"

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.160
The Last Exorcism

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.420
How did The Last Exorcism, the found-footage
possession pic that's appeared on many a "scariest

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.299
horror films" list slip by with a PG-13 rating?

00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:17.129
This genuinely eerie 2010 film begins with
Reverend Cotton Marcus embarking on what he

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:20.380
thinks will be a routine fake exorcism he's
grown used to performing.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:25.660
Here's just a taste of what then goes down:
there's face slashing, animal killing, and

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:26.719
finger breaking.

00:03:26.719 --> 00:03:30.680
There are horrifying hooded figures, decapitations,
and people getting burned alive.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.900
And, of course, there's a possessed girl who
contorts into a human pretzel and fills an

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.860
already eerie barn with the sounds of her
strained, demonic voice.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.160
"We're gonna go now, we're gonna get you in
the car…"

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.580
[Scream]

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:44.640
"Are you okay?"

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.240
Drag Me to Hell

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.040
Director Sam Raimi returned to his horror
roots with 2009's Drag Me to Hell.

00:03:53.049 --> 00:03:57.190
The film begins as mild-mannered bank loan
officer Christine Brown turns down her client

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.900
Sylvia's request for yet another mortgage
extension.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.820
On the verge of eviction, Sylvia crawls into
the back seat of Christine's car, then attacks

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.040
and places a curse on her.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.320
Now haunted by a soul-starved spirit, Christine's
life spirals into a blood-soaked horror show.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.500
She imagines flies buzzing in her stomach,
experiences a projectile nosebleed, takes

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:21.590
part in a demonic goat sacrifice, jumps into
a grave to dig up a corpse, and gets embalming

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.900
liquid pumped into her mouth via a dead person's
vomit.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.840
Featuring some of the most ferociously gruesome

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:37.240
gags in recent memory, Drag Me to Hell is
a hammy but horrifying splatter-fest that

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.760
is somehow not rated R.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.180
The Ring

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:46.020
2002's The Ring is intensely terrifying with
a weird concept: watch a VHS tape and die

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.370
seven days later.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:51.960
It's only made odder and more unsettling by
helmer Gore Verbinski's off-kilter directorial

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:52.460
choices.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.699
Dead bodies and the disturbing videotape connect
a handful of Pacific Northwest teenagers to

00:04:57.699 --> 00:05:01.590
journalist Rachel Keller, who ventures to
find out the truth behind the killings and

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.610
see if she can escape the unavoidable.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:08.460
The entire film is filled with grisly images,
most notably drowned ghost Samara Morgan emerging

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.520
from a TV screen and staggering across the
floor.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:15.620
There's also a horse getting chopped to pieces
by the blades of a ferry propeller, plus some

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.490
disembowelment and ripped-up fingernails for
good measure.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:23.449
What ultimately pushes The Ring into should-be-R-rated
territory is its continuous sense of terror

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:27.430
and persistent disturbing imagery that leave
you with a feeling of dread you just can't

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:27.930
shake.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.060
"Oh my God, Katie…

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.400
You freak!"

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:37.040
Jaws

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:42.340
This 1975 Steven Spielberg classic sees a
gung-ho group of guys journey into the big

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.380
blue in search of the man-eating great white
shark that's been terrorizing beachgoers on

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.020
Amity Island.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:51.660
Things go just about as well as you'd anticipate
they would in a shark-hunting venture.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.930
The inclusion of many brutal fatalities and
the explosive shark death makes Jaws completely

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.720
inappropriate for the tame PG rating it was
given.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:04.240
Even though the MPAA had, at the time, only
PG or R to pick when rating Jaws, the clear

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.360
choice should have been the latter.

